    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n# \n ![](https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7dad02d007830a346454923713608dcb?d=retro&size=100) ⟨28⟩\nINCModel2⟨28⟩\n/\nHy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview⟨29⟩\nlike 1\nFollow\n![⟨30⟩] INC Optimized Models 2 5\n Text Generation ⟨31⟩ Transformers ⟨32⟩ Safetensors ⟨33⟩ hy_v3 ⟨34⟩ auto-round ⟨35⟩ conversational ⟨36⟩ 8-bit precision ⟨37⟩ compressed-tensors ⟨38⟩\narxiv: 2309.05516\nLicense: apache-2.0\n Model card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨39⟩ Community ⟨40⟩\nDeploy\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this model\n### Instructions to use INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n  * Libraries\n  *  Transformers⟨41⟩\nHow to use INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview with Transformers:\n\n```\n# Use a pipeline as a high-level helper\nfrom transformers import pipeline\n\npipe = pipeline(\"text-generation\", model=\"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\")\nmessages = [\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Who are you?\"},\n]\npipe(messages)\n```\n\n```\n# Load model directly\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\")\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\", device_map=\"auto\")\nmessages = [\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Who are you?\"},\n]\ninputs = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n\tmessages,\n\tadd_generation_prompt=True,\n\ttokenize=True,\n\treturn_dict=True,\n\treturn_tensors=\"pt\",\n).to(model.device)\n\noutputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=40)\nprint(tokenizer.decode(outputs[0][inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[-1]:]))\n```\n\n  * Notebooks\n  *  Google Colab⟨42⟩\n  *  Kaggle⟨43⟩\n  * Local Apps Settings⟨44⟩\n  *  vLLM ⟨45⟩\nHow to use INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview with vLLM:\n##### Install from pip and serve model\n\n```\n# Install vLLM from pip:\npip install vllm\n# Start the vLLM server:\nvllm serve \"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\"\n# Call the server using curl (OpenAI-compatible API):\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions\" \\\n\t-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n\t--data '{\n\t\t\"model\": \"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\",\n\t\t\"messages\": [\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\",\n\t\t\t\t\"content\": \"What is the capital of France?\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t]\n\t}'\n```\n\n##### Use Docker\n\n```\ndocker model run hf.co/INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\n```\n\n  *  SGLang ⟨46⟩\nHow to use INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview with SGLang:\n##### Install from pip and serve model\n\n```\n# Install SGLang from pip:\npip install sglang\n# Start the SGLang server:\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n    --model-path \"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\" \\\n    --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n    --port 30000\n# Call the server using curl (OpenAI-compatible API):\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:30000/v1/chat/completions\" \\\n\t-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n\t--data '{\n\t\t\"model\": \"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\",\n\t\t\"messages\": [\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\",\n\t\t\t\t\"content\": \"What is the capital of France?\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t]\n\t}'\n```\n\n##### Use Docker images\n\n```\ndocker run --gpus all \\\n    --shm-size 32g \\\n    -p 30000:30000 \\\n    -v ~/.cache/huggingface:/root/.cache/huggingface \\\n    --env \"HF_TOKEN=<secret>\" \\\n    --ipc=host \\\n    lmsysorg/sglang:latest \\\n    python3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\n        --model-path \"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\" \\\n        --host 0.0.0.0 \\\n        --port 30000\n# Call the server using curl (OpenAI-compatible API):\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:30000/v1/chat/completions\" \\\n\t-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n\t--data '{\n\t\t\"model\": \"INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\",\n\t\t\"messages\": [\n\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\"role\": \"user\",\n\t\t\t\t\"content\": \"What is the capital of France?\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t]\n\t}'\n```\n\n  *  Docker Model Runner ⟨47⟩\nHow to use INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview with Docker Model Runner:\n\n```\ndocker model run hf.co/INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\n```\n\n\n\n  * Model Details⟨48⟩\n  * Generate the Model⟨49⟩\n  * Ethical Considerations and Limitations⟨50⟩\n  * Caveats and Recommendations⟨51⟩\n  * Disclaimer⟨52⟩\n  * Cite⟨53⟩\n\n\n##   ⟨48⟩ Model Details \nThis model is a MXFP4 and MXFP8 mixed model of tencent/Hy3⟨54⟩ generated by intel/auto-round⟨55⟩ with RTN mode. The model format is Compressed Tensor (CT), fully compatible with vLLM.\n##   ⟨49⟩ Generate the Model \nRTN version\n\n```\nauto-round tencent/Hy3  --model_free --scheme MXFP8 --format llm_compressor --layer_config \"{mlp.experts:{scheme:MXFP4}}\" --output_dir /workspace/models/tencent/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨50⟩ Ethical Considerations and Limitations \nThe model can produce factually incorrect output, and should not be relied on to produce factually accurate information. Because of the limitations of the pretrained model and the finetuning datasets, it is possible that this model could generate lewd, biased or otherwise offensive outputs.\nTherefore, before deploying any applications of the model, developers should perform safety testing.\n##   ⟨51⟩ Caveats and Recommendations \nUsers (both direct and downstream) should be made aware of the risks, biases and limitations of the model.\nHere are a couple of useful links to learn more about Intel's AI software:\n  * Intel Neural Compressor⟨56⟩\n\n\n##   ⟨52⟩ Disclaimer \nThe license on this model does not constitute legal advice. We are not responsible for the actions of third parties who use this model. Please consult an attorney before using this model for commercial purposes.\n##   ⟨53⟩ Cite \n@article{cheng2023optimize, title={Optimize weight rounding via signed gradient descent for the quantization of llms}, author={Cheng, Wenhua and Zhang, Weiwei and Shen, Haihao and Cai, Yiyang and He, Xin and Lv, Kaokao and Liu, Yi}, journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2309.05516}, year={2023} }\narxiv⟨57⟩ github⟨55⟩ \n\nDownloads last month\n    1,461\nSafetensors⟨58⟩\nModel size\n163B params\nTensor type\nF8_E4M3 \n·\nU8 \n·\nBF16 \n·\nF32 \n·\nChat template\nFiles info\nInference Providers NEW⟨59⟩\n Text Generation ⟨60⟩\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. 🙋 Ask for provider support⟨61⟩\n##  Model tree for INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview ⟨62⟩\nBase model\ntencent/Hy3⟨54⟩\nQuantized\n(68⟨63⟩)\nthis model\n##  Paper for INCModel2/Hy3-MXFP4-Mixed-CT-AutoRound-Preview\n#### Optimize Weight Rounding via Signed Gradient Descent for the Quantization of LLMs Paper • 2309.05516 • Published Sep 11, 2023 • 13 ⟨64⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨65⟩ Privacy⟨66⟩ About⟨67⟩ Careers⟨68⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
